1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:04,971
OFE-GUI can run your fits on
another computer: a workstation,

2
00:00:04,971 --> 00:00:07,742
a lab server, or a virtual machine.

3
00:00:07,892 --> 00:00:11,905
Your browser stays on your computer,
and the fitting happens over there.

4
00:00:12,055 --> 00:00:17,394
This tour starts with the -ssh option,
and then shows the alternatives.

5
00:00:18,894 --> 00:00:20,150
On its own,

6
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:26,541
OFE-GUI runs on your computer
and opens in your browser,

7
00:00:26,541 --> 00:00:29,631
at 127.0.0.1, port 8143.

8
00:00:29,781 --> 00:00:33,237
It has no login, and it can
browse files and run fits,

9
00:00:33,237 --> 00:00:35,828
so it never listens on the network.

10
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:42,284
To reach another computer, it uses SSH:
your account, your keys and your settings.

11
00:00:43,784 --> 00:00:44,500
With -ssh,

12
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:50,648
one command starts OFE-GUI on the remote
account and connects your browser to it.

13
00:00:50,798 --> 00:00:55,299
Name the remote programs, and
the OFE_PATH their engine needs.

14
00:00:55,449 --> 00:01:00,820
-remote-dir picks the folder it starts in,
and -enable-terminal adds the Terminal.

15
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:05,676
The launcher forwards port 8143
on your computer through SSH,

16
00:01:05,676 --> 00:01:08,263
and opens it in your browser.

17
00:01:09,763 --> 00:01:12,934
Everything on this page now
runs on the remote host.

18
00:01:13,084 --> 00:01:18,598
The Terminal is a shell on forky, an
arm64 server, in the folder we chose.

19
00:01:18,748 --> 00:01:22,657
Choose files uploads data from
your computer into that folder;

20
00:01:22,657 --> 00:01:25,655
Choose on forky picks files already there.

21
00:01:25,805 --> 00:01:34,378
The fit runs there too, with the same
result: T1 is 1.998, plus or minus 0.030.

22
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:38,304
A few options shape the remote session.

23
00:01:38,454 --> 00:01:43,820
Give each account or server its own remote
address, so that sessions never collide.

24
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:49,394
An idle timeout stops the remote OFE-GUI
once nobody has used it for a while.

25
00:01:49,544 --> 00:01:56,476
Your SSH configuration applies as usual:
host aliases, keys, agents and jump hosts.

26
00:01:56,626 --> 00:01:59,286
Close the launcher, or
lose the connection,

27
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:01,678
and the remote OFE-GUI stops too.

28
00:02:03,178 --> 00:02:05,955
-connect-remote divides
the work differently.

29
00:02:06,105 --> 00:02:08,462
OFE-GUI runs on your computer,

30
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:12,469
and a second OFE-GUI is
started on the remote host,

31
00:02:12,469 --> 00:02:14,469
behind an SSH tunnel.

32
00:02:14,619 --> 00:02:18,308
The launcher reports both,
each on its own address.

33
00:02:19,808 --> 00:02:24,072
In Settings, the Remote onefite-gui
field already holds the tunnel's address.

34
00:02:24,222 --> 00:02:28,674
The Terminal and the files stay on
your computer, here in the fits folder.

35
00:02:28,824 --> 00:02:32,811
Only the fit goes to the remote
host, and its results come back here.

36
00:02:32,961 --> 00:02:36,256
Clear the field, and the
next fit runs locally.

37
00:02:37,756 --> 00:02:40,346
If OFE-GUI already runs on the server,

38
00:02:40,346 --> 00:02:44,648
for example as a system service,
open the tunnel yourself.

39
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:49,379
Then open its address in
your browser, as with -ssh,

40
00:02:49,529 --> 00:02:53,219
or put it in the Remote onefite-gui
field of your own OFE-GUI,

41
00:02:53,219 --> 00:02:54,998
as with -connect-remote.

42
00:02:56,498 --> 00:03:01,391
Sometimes the computer that runs the
fits is behind NAT or a firewall,

43
00:03:01,391 --> 00:03:03,768
and can't accept connections.

44
00:03:03,918 --> 00:03:05,293
With -reverse-ssh,

45
00:03:05,293 --> 00:03:09,496
it serves OFE-GUI itself and
opens the tunnel outbound,

46
00:03:09,496 --> 00:03:11,986
to a computer you can reach.

47
00:03:12,136 --> 00:03:19,520
On that computer, open 127.0.0.1,
port 8143, in the browser.

48
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,937
OFE-GUI can also drive an
engine web service directly:

49
00:03:24,937 --> 00:03:29,421
in Settings, give the onefite
executable an http address.

50
00:03:29,571 --> 00:03:34,608
That service comes from the Raku engine,
started with onefite start-web-engine.

51
00:03:34,758 --> 00:03:36,556
Its interface is smaller:

52
00:03:36,556 --> 00:03:39,434
one data file per fit and fewer options,

53
00:03:39,434 --> 00:03:44,172
and anything unsupported is
reported, never silently dropped.

54
00:03:45,672 --> 00:03:48,044
So choose by where things should run.

55
00:03:48,194 --> 00:03:51,532
-ssh puts everything on the remote host.

56
00:03:51,682 --> 00:03:55,903
-connect-remote keeps the interface
here, and sends the fits there.

57
00:03:56,053 --> 00:03:59,674
A tunnel reaches an OFE-GUI
that is already running.

58
00:03:59,824 --> 00:04:04,009
-reverse-ssh works when the
fitting machine can't be reached.

59
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:10,861
In every case OFE-GUI listens only on
127.0.0.1, and SSH does the connecting.

60
00:04:12,361 --> 00:04:17,035
onefite-gui -h lists every option, and
its manual page describes them all.

